            <ArticleTitle>Radioiodine associated de novo Graves' opthalmopathy in an Asian cohort.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-231</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1967/s002449910606</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Radioactive iodine in the treatment of Graves' disease has been associated with the development of de novo Graves' ophthalmopathy (GO). In this report, we describe five individuals who required extensive ophthalmic treatment for post-RAI de novo GO.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
